<div style="line-height:11.0pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:6pt;"><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial;font-size:9pt;">The after-tax returns presented in the table below are calculated using highest historical
individual federal marginal income tax rates </font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial;font-size:9pt;">and do not reflect the impact of state and local taxes. </font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial;font-size:9pt;">Your actual
after-tax returns will depend on your specific tax situation and may </font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial;font-size:9pt;">differ from those shown below. After-tax returns are not relevant to investors who hold Fund Shares through
tax-advantaged </font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial;font-size:9pt;">arrangements, such as 401(k) plans or individual retirement accounts. </font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial;font-size:9pt;">The returns after taxes can
exceed the returns before taxes </font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial;font-size:9pt;">due to an assumed tax benefit for a shareholder from realizing a capital loss on a sale of Fund Shares.</font><font
style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial;font-size:1pt;line-height:1pt;">&#8195;</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:1.0pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:6pt;"> </div> </div> <div style="margin-top:0.0pt;">
